{
  "_": [
    "jaws_le on JPSalas & marty's 'JAWS 50th Anniversary' 3.2, a scripted original:",
    "vpxshadow.py keeps its script as a shadow game and hands the ball to the real",
    "game. The LE card, not the Pro: the table has the LE's fourth flipper (the upper",
    "one, LeftFlipperG, on the right button as Stern's UP P/F R FLIP is) and its shark",
    "rising out of the lagoon (the Targetshark drop targets, raised by the SHARK MOTOR",
    "coil here). The lower playfield's inserts sit where Stern's do (the drawing fits",
    "X = (x - 15) * 3.34, Y = (y - 15) * 3.13 below the boat); the upper third is JP's",
    "own layout, so the switches up there are matched by what the script does with",
    "them and the GUESS ones want a look at the machine. The table has no eject coils",
    "(neither has the machine): its kickers keep their own script (orig_keep).",
    "Ids: the RIG's switch_list.txt for jaws_le; coils through group_node.txt (group",
    "7 = node 8, group 8 = node 9).",
    "GI: the LE names no playfield GI LEDs, so the table's own GIUpdateTimer keeps its",
    "GI on (not quieted); its attract shows, rainbow and insert effects are."
  ],
